# =============================================================================
# full_suite · 01 — ACQUIRE & DOCUMENT           (Stage 1 of the hydrology study)
# =============================================================================
# Study : past & present hydrologic assessment of the Youngstown AOI.
#         Full brief, methods, and references → use_case.md (read that first).
#
# THIS STAGE
#   1. Build a light, SHIPPED study-area visualization from examples/demo/ so the
#      example opens with a map of Youngstown — no download required to *see* it.
#   2. DOCUMENT every raw input (catalog + assess) into outputs/notes/ — the
#      quality + provenance record a scientific Methods section needs.
#
# SHIPPED vs FETCHED  (see use_case.md § "Shipped vs fetched")
#   * SHIPPED (in the repo, from ../demo/): AOI, village, hydrography, hillshade.
#   * FETCHED from primary sources into read-only inputs/ by the companion script
#     (OUTSIDE niva, since niva has no `fetch` verb yet — candidate in ../../TODO.md):
#         bash fetch_inputs.sh        # LiDAR 3DEP · NLCD 2001/2021 · WBD HUC12 · hist ortho
#     Raw is never modified: this flow only READS inputs/ and only WRITES to
#     derived/ and outputs/.
#
# PROVIDERS : native → gdal → GRASS (only where needed) → PDAL (pdalcli:). No SAGA/OTB.
# RUN (headless): export QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen ; export NIVA_TMPDIR=/var/tmp/niva
#      journal the exact processing chain:  export NIVA_LOG=outputs/notes/journal/01_acquire
#      then:  cd examples/full_suite && niva run 01_acquire.niva
# =============================================================================

# PROGRESS NOTIFICATIONS (optional) — the `notify` steps in this flow are COMMENTED
# OUT so the example runs with zero setup. Uncomment them to push progress pings via
# ntfy; `notify` needs a topic (set NIVA_NTFY_TOPIC, or the plugin Setup tab, or add
# `to=<topic>` to the call). Message variables you can interpolate: {now} clock time ·
# {elapsed} total job time · {last} previous step's time · {ops} ops run · {errors}
# error count. `priority=high` flags the important pings. (v0.40's render heartbeat +
# the NIVA_LOG journal also show progress without ntfy.)
# notify "niva full_suite · 01 acquire — start {now}" priority=high   # start ping

# --- 0 · package skeleton --------------------------------------------------
# No mkdir verb needed: inputs/ derived/ outputs/{data,notes,figures,tables,report}
# are auto-created by the first save/catalog/assess that targets them.

# --- 1 · SHIPPED study-area visualization (from ../demo/, light) -----------
# Reproject the shipped context layers to the study SRS (EPSG:6346) into derived/,
# then compose a locator map. These are the only "processing" writes this stage
# makes; everything heavy is fetched + documented, not transformed, here.
#
# CONVENTION (whole study): every processing step also saves a `figure` — a quick,
# pass-through PNG of its output into outputs/figures/ — as a visual audit trail.
# `figure` is pass-through, so it chains right after `save`. Composed `map` layouts
# (below) are produced as needed for the report.
load "../demo/demo.gpkg|layername=aoi"            | reproject EPSG:6346 | save derived/aoi_6346.gpkg | figure outputs/figures/01_aoi.png
load "../demo/demo.gpkg|layername=ny_youngstown"  | reproject EPSG:6346 | save derived/village_6346.gpkg | figure outputs/figures/01_village.png
load "../demo/demo.gpkg|layername=ytown_nhdflowline" | reproject EPSG:6346 | fixgeom | save derived/hydro_6346.gpkg | figure outputs/figures/01_hydro.png
load "../demo/hillshade.tif"                      | warp EPSG:6346       | save derived/hillshade_6346.tif | figure outputs/figures/01_hillshade.png

# Composed cartographic locator (legend + scale bar + north arrow are on by default).
# One stage = one line (niva has no line-continuation). Self-contained (hillshade
# base); add `basemap=osm` for a web base map (needs network).
load derived/hillshade_6346.tif | map outputs/figures/00_study_area.png title="Youngstown AOI — Niagara River & Lake Ontario waterfronts" layers="derived/hydro_6346.gpkg;derived/village_6346.gpkg;derived/aoi_6346.gpkg" dpi=200
# notify "01 · shipped study-area map ready ({elapsed})"   # progress ping after the locator map

# --- 2 · DOCUMENT the SHIPPED layers (always available — no fetch needed) ---
# The parcels + hydrography that drive §2–§5 come from the shipped demo gpkg;
# document them (deep assess on parcels — 2,790 features, rich schema):
load "../demo/demo.gpkg|layername=parcels"       | assess --deep to outputs/notes/quality_parcels.md
load "../demo/demo.gpkg|layername=ny_streams"    | assess to outputs/notes/quality_streams.md

# --- 3 · DOCUMENT the FETCHED inputs — REQUIRES `bash fetch_inputs.sh` first -
# fetch_inputs.sh populates read-only inputs/ and records source/URL/date/sha256
# to outputs/notes/provenance_inputs.md. Everything below reads that raw tree; a
# no-fetch run stops here (by design) having still produced the study-area map and
# the shipped-layer docs above.
catalog "inputs" to="outputs/notes/catalog_inputs.md"
# per-dataset quality profile (CRS set? extent, schema, validity, dupes, nulls,
# lineage) — writes a report, alters nothing:
load "inputs/ortho_2024/porter_ortho.jp2"        | assess to outputs/notes/quality_ortho_2024.md
load "inputs/nlcd/nlcd_impervious_2021.tif"      | assess to outputs/notes/quality_nlcd_2021.md
load "inputs/nlcd/nlcd_impervious_2001.tif"      | assess to outputs/notes/quality_nlcd_2001.md
load "inputs/huc12/huc12.gpkg"                   | assess to outputs/notes/quality_huc12.md
load "inputs/ortho_hist/porter_hist.tif"         | assess to outputs/notes/quality_ortho_hist.md
# LiDAR point clouds: catalog the folder (per-tile CRS/extent/point counts):
catalog "inputs/lidar" to="outputs/notes/catalog_lidar.md"

# --- done ------------------------------------------------------------------
# notify "niva full_suite · 01 acquire complete ✓ ({elapsed}) — inputs documented, map rendered" priority=high
# Provenance (fetch_inputs.sh) + catalogs + assessments now sit in outputs/notes/,
# and a study-area figure in outputs/figures/. Next: 02_prepare.niva (reproject/
# clip everything to the AOI in EPSG:6346 → derived/, still leaving inputs/ raw).
